    "origin_id": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/hayesx-250-is-the-newest-american-personal-evtol-born-in-las-vegas-278050.html",
    "canonical_url": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/hayesx-250-is-the-newest-american-personal-evtol-born-in-las-vegas-278050.html",
    "origin_publisher": "autoevolution",
    "published_at": "2026-11-06T08:56:54+00:00",
    "published_at_raw": "2026-11-06T08:56:54+0000",
    "publication_precision": "TIMESTAMP",
    "acquired_at": "2026-11-06T09:04:04.324423+00:00",
    "available_at": "2026-11-06T09:04:04.324423+00:00",
    "body": "2026 SEMA Show • SRT Performance Joins the 2026 SEMA Show Featuring the First-Ever Jeep Wrangler Scrambler Concept\nHayesX-250 Is the Newest American Personal eVTOL, Born in Las Vegas\n9 photos\nPhoto: HayesX/Instagram\nIf you have been dreaming of an US-built personal eVTOL (electric vertical takeoff and landing) that allows you to fly without a pilot license and that can be delivered to you relatively fast, now is your chance – the brand-new HayesX-250 checks all of these boxes and is available for order, with a limited number of deliveries as soon as this year.\nThere are different types of electric aircraft marketed as personal eVTOLs, but a very limited number of those fall under the FAA (Federal Aviation Administration) Part 103 regulations – meaning single-seat vehicles under 254 lbs (empty) and with a maximum speed of 63 mph.\nThe most popular in this category worldwide is, no doubt, the Jetson One, originally developed in Europe. Another personal eVTOL in this category is the Chinese CoolFly Dream , introduced to the US market earlier this year, when it was on display at EAA AirVenture Oshkosh. Now, the newest name to join the ranks of this very exclusive club is HayesX, with its flagship aircraft, the HayesX-250.\nYou’ll notice that all three have very similar designs, centered around the single-seat configuration and an ultra-compact, but extremely protective shell. Their specifications are also very similar, since they all fall in line with the required FAA Part 103 requirements for maximum weight, speed, and so on.\nThe HayesX-250, which is making its official debut at this year’s SEMA Show at the Las Vegas Convention Center (4-6 November, 2026), is also priced almost the same as the ultra-popular Jetson One. The HayesX-250 can be ordered for $146,600, with a $6,000 deposit, while the Jetson One is priced at $148,000, with an $8,000 deposit.\nThe huge difference right now is in how fast you can get your hands on this personal eVTOL. The Las Vegas-based company is currently accepting a limited number of orders for 2026 delivery, which is incredibly fast, while the Jetson One production is already sold out for 2026 and 2027, with earliest deliveries available only in 2028.\nIn addition to an aviation-grade aluminum chassis, and an eight-electric motor configuration, this personal eVTOL comes with two big advantages. One is the multi-layered system redundancy and safety features, including a whole-aircraft ballistic parachute, with a clearance as low as ten meters (32.8 feet). The other is an ultra-compact design with folding arms, that allows easy transportation of the aircraft in a pickup or trailer.\nWhat makes the HayesX-250 extra appealing is its versatility in terms of potential applications. Although technically a personal eVTOL, this single-seat vehicle isn’t meant just for leisure flights.\nIt can become an awesome work buddy for folks working in farm management, land development, and even search-and-rescue. From advanced aerial photography to emergency first aid, this lightweight, compact aircraft can prove to be highly useful, not just fun.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nHayesX-250 HayesX personal eVTOL personal aircraft evtol electric aircraft\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Otilia Drăgan\nOtilia believes that if it’s eco, green, or groundbreaking, people should know about it (especially if it's got wheels or wings). Working in online media for over five years, she's gained a deeper perspective on how people everywhere can inspire each other. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1,300-HP C6 Corvette 427 Turbo Hits 200 Mph in Fourth Gear, Packs Classic 6-Speed Manual Tranny",
